.sd.gov/News/2026/05082026.aspx","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/dockets/electric/2025/EL25-024/Redline120125.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section3/1.pdf","https://taxcloud.com/sales-tax-radar/south-dakota-sales-tax-rate-increase-in-2027/"]},"export":{"method":"instant","buyback_cents_kwh":3.16,"extra_monthly_charge":3.75,"notes":"South Dakota has no net metering. Xcel buys what the house does not use at the moment it is made at 3.16 cents/kWh (small-generator tariff E50, 2026) and adds a $3.75/month metering charge; solar used in the house as it is made saves the full retail rate.","sources":["https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section9/1.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section9/2.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section9/3.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section9/4.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/Tariffs/Electric/Xcel/section9/6.pdf","https://puc.sd.gov/Publications/solarfaq.aspx","https://sdlegislature.gov/Rules/Administrative/20:10:36:06","https://sdlegislature.gov/Rules/Administrative/20:10:36:31","https://sdlegislature.gov/Rules/Administrative/20:10:36:27","https://puc.sd.gov/commission/commissionaction/interconnectionreports/2025XcelReport.pdf"]},"federal":{"itc_25d_available":false,"notes":"P.L. 119-21 (OBBBA, signed 2025-07-04) sec. 70506 terminated the IRC 25D Residential Clean Energy Credit for expenditures made after 2025-12-31. Per IRC 25D(e)(8) and IRS FAQ, an expenditure is treated as made when original installation is completed, so a homeowner-owned system completed in late 2026/2027 gets no 25D credit even if paid for in 2025. Unused 25D credit from 2025-or-earlier installs can still carry forward. Remaining federal route: third-party-owned (lease/PPA) residential solar can still use the business credits 45Y/48E, provided the project begins construction by 2026-07-04 (then has a multi-year placed-in-service window) or is placed in service by 2027-12-31; FEOC sourcing restrictions also apply from 2026. Any lessor credit benefit reaches the homeowner only indirectly through lease pricing. No federal credit for a homeowner-owned system in this scenario.","sources":["https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/faqs-for-modification-of-sections-25c-25d-25e-30c-30d-45l-45w-and-179d-under-public-law-119-21-139-stat-72-july-4-2025-commonly-known-as-the-one-big-beautiful-bill-act-obbb","https://www.everycrsreport.com/reports/IN12611.html","https://www.crowe.com/insights/new-clean-energy-tax-provisions-and-what-laws-are-changing","https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2025/07/how-does-hr1-change-the-residential-solar-itc/","https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2026/feb/navigating-safe-harbor-rules-for-solar-and-wind-sec-48e-facilities.html"]},"installed_cost_per_w":{"low":2.6,"typical":3.25,"high":3.8}},"usage":{"annual_avg":750,"shape":[1325,1266,1058,842,763,844,1063,1010,836,798,860,1150],"notes":"Default 750 kWh a month (the average Xcel South Dakota home, per the PUC) shaped like EIA 2025 South Dakota monthly use; type your own from your bill."},"assumptions":{"daytime_share":0.45,"panel_per_w":0.45,"inverter_per_w":0.35,"racking_per_w":0.15,"bos_per_w":0.25,"permit_fixed":400,"notes":"Self-use is estimated from monthly totals (about 45 % of a home's use falls in daylight hours), not an hourly simulation. Parts not sold at either store (grid-tie inverter, roof racking, wiring) are priced per watt as estimates."}}